IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `niis-dates`
IMPORT `niis-core`

-- National Injury Insurance Scheme (Queensland) Act 2016 -- the scheme for treatment, care and support after a serious
-- motor accident injury in Queensland, from the seat of the injured person.
--
-- SEAT: the injured person: someone seriously injured in a motor accident in Queensland (spinal cord, brain, amputation,
-- brachial plexus, burns, blindness), who applies to the scheme or is a participant in it; or a parent, guardian or
-- other person acting for them. "Does the scheme cover me? Am I eligible? Can I apply, and must the agency take my
-- application? By when must it decide? How long is my interim participation, and what happens at its end? Will the
-- agency pay this expense, how much, and by when must I ask? I am also claiming damages from the CTP insurer: what must I
-- tell the agency, and by when; do I keep my right to treatment, care and support damages? I am going overseas: what
-- must I do? How do I get a decision reviewed, and by when? What can I be penalised for?" Every question is asked as the
-- injured person would ask it, on facts they can state; the agency's, the insurer's and the court's decisions are facts
-- they answer from what they have been told. The rules are in niis-core.l4; this module builds their inputs from plain
-- answers and restates no rule. Inputs with the same meaning have the same name in every question.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Injury Insurance Scheme (Queensland) Act 2016 -- the injured person's questions`

-- A placeholder for a date the question's rule does not read.
`a date not used` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000

DECLARE `Who may apply answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, this person may apply for me`
    `yes, the insurer may apply for me, and must give me a copy of the application (s 18(2))`
    `no: an insurer may apply only while its claim for my injury is not finalised (s 18(1)(a))`
    `the Act does not settle whether this person may apply for me`

DECLARE `Application deadline answer` IS ONE OF
    `the application period ends on` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

§§ `Does the scheme cover me (ss 4, 7, 12, 13 and schedule 1)`

@export Does the National Injury Insurance Scheme (Queensland) Act 2016 apply to my injury from a motor accident?
GIVEN `my injury` IS AN `Injury` @desc Which of the Act's serious personal injuries you have: a permanent spinal cord injury with permanent neurological deficit; a traumatic brain injury with permanent impairment; a forequarter or shoulder disarticulation amputation; a leg amputation through or above the femur; amputation of more than 1 limb or parts of different limbs; a permanent brachial plexus injury equivalent to a shoulder disarticulation amputation; a full thickness burn; an inhalation burn with permanent respiratory impairment; permanent blindness caused by trauma; or another personal injury
      `the vehicle` IS A `Vehicle` @desc The vehicle that caused the injury: a motor vehicle with CTP insurance in force; a trailer with CTP insurance or covered by one; a vehicle owned by a self-insurer (the Commonwealth, or another State that does not insure its vehicles); a trailer a self-insurer would cover; an uninsured motor vehicle or uninsured trailer covered by a nominal defendant scheme; an unidentified vehicle covered by a nominal defendant scheme; or none of these
      `how my injury happened` IS A `How the injury happened` @desc How the vehicle caused the injury: by its driving; by a collision with it, or action taken to avoid one; by it running out of control; by a defect causing loss of control while it was driven; or some other way
      `the kind of vehicle` IS A `Kind of vehicle` @desc Whether the vehicle was mobile machinery (tractor, backhoe, bulldozer, end-loader, forklift, crane or hoist), an agricultural machine in agricultural use, a rail or tram vehicle, an amphibious vehicle, a vehicle prescribed by regulation, or an ordinary vehicle
      `where the accident happened` IS A `Where it happened` @desc Where the accident happened: on a road; in a public place that is not a road; or somewhere else (for example private land)
      `the accident happened in Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor accident happened in Queensland
      `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `the vehicle was used for terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was being used, at the time, to commit or threaten an act of terrorism (almost always no)
GIVETH AN `Application of the Act`
DECIDE `Does the Act apply to my injury` IS
    `the s 4 answer` `my injury` `the vehicle` `how my injury happened` `the kind of vehicle` `where the accident happened` `the accident happened in Queensland` `the day of my accident` `the vehicle was used for terrorism`

@export Am I eligible to participate in Queensland's national injury insurance scheme for my serious motor accident injury?
GIVEN `my injury` IS AN `Injury` @desc Which of the Act's serious personal injuries you have (see the first question), or another personal injury
      `the vehicle` IS A `Vehicle` @desc The vehicle that caused the injury and how it was insured (see the first question)
      `how my injury happened` IS A `How the injury happened` @desc How the vehicle caused the injury (see the first question)
      `the kind of vehicle` IS A `Kind of vehicle` @desc The kind of vehicle (see the first question)
      `where the accident happened` IS A `Where it happened` @desc Where the accident happened: on a road; in a public place that is not a road; or somewhere else
      `the accident happened in Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor accident happened in Queensland
      `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `the vehicle was used for terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was being used for an act of terrorism (almost always no)
      `my injury meets the eligibility criteria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury meets the eligibility criteria the National Injury Insurance Scheme (Queensland) Regulation sets for it (the agency decides this; a medical tribunal can review it)
      `I was awarded damages for my care needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court judgment or binding settlement has already awarded you damages for your treatment, care and support needs from this injury
      `those damages were paid other than by the agency under s 44(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those damages were paid by someone other than the agency under s 44(3)(a) (for example by the CTP insurer)
      `I had another injury or condition before the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you already had another injury or condition before the accident
      `the accident permanently increased my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the serious injury permanently increased the disability you had before the accident (answer yes if you had none)
GIVETH AN `Eligibility`
DECIDE `Am I eligible to participate in the scheme` IS
    `the s 12 answer`
        ((`the s 4 answer` `my injury` `the vehicle` `how my injury happened` `the kind of vehicle` `where the accident happened` `the accident happened in Queensland` `the day of my accident` `the vehicle was used for terrorism`) EQUALS `the Act applies to the injury`)
        `my injury meets the eligibility criteria` `I was awarded damages for my care needs` `those damages were paid other than by the agency under s 44(3)(a)` `I had another injury or condition before the accident` `the accident permanently increased my disability`

@export I am not eligible for the national injury insurance scheme: can I buy into it under s 13?
GIVEN `I am eligible under s 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are eligible to participate in the scheme in the ordinary way (the eligibility question)
      `my injury is prescribed for buying in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury is one the regulation prescribes for buying into the scheme
GIVETH A `Buy-in`
DECIDE `Can I buy into the scheme` IS
    `the s 13 answer` `I am eligible under s 12` `my injury is prescribed for buying in`

@export I was accepted as a buy-in participant: have I paid my contribution in time, or have I stopped being a participant?
GIVEN `the day I was accepted` IS A DATE @desc The day the agency accepted you as a buy-in participant
      `I have paid my contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the buy-in contribution
      `the day I paid it` IS A DATE @desc The day you paid it (any date if you have not)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you want the answer for, usually today
GIVETH A `Buy-in standing`
DECIDE `Am I still a buy-in participant` IS
    `the s 13(4) answer` `the day I was accepted` `I have paid my contribution` `the day I paid it` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `Applying to the scheme (ss 10, 16-18)`

@export By when should I apply to the national injury insurance scheme so that the agency must accept my application?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
GIVETH AN `Application deadline answer`
DECIDE `By when should I apply` IS
    `the application period ends on` (`the last day of the application period (s 16(2))` `the day of my accident`)

@export Must the National Injury Insurance Agency accept my application, or may it decide not to because it is late?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or will make) the application
      `I received a s 44(3)(a) payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or someone for you) have already received a payment from the agency under s 44(3)(a) for accepting awarded treatment, care and support damages
GIVETH AN `Acceptance of the application`
DECIDE `Must the agency accept my application` IS
    `the s 16 answer` `the day of my accident` `the day I apply` `I received a s 44(3)(a) payment`

@export Can an application to the national injury insurance scheme be made for my injury now?
GIVEN `another application for my injury is undecided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone else has applied for your injury and the agency has not yet decided
      `I am an interim participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are now an interim participant in the scheme for this injury
      `an earlier application was refused or my interim participation ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier application for this injury was refused, or your interim participation for it has ended
      `I give new or deterioration medical information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you will give the agency medical information it has not considered before, or showing your condition has got worse since then
      `I received a s 44(3)(a) payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have received a payment from the agency under s 44(3)(a) for this injury
      `the day I received the payment` IS A DATE @desc The day you received that payment (any date if none)
      `the years the regulation sets after a payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The waiting period, in whole years, the regulation prescribes after a s 44(3)(a) payment (the Act says at least 5; give 5 if you do not know)
      `the regulation's circumstances apply to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in the circumstances the regulation prescribes for applying again after a s 44(3)(a) payment (answer yes if you received no payment)
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you want to apply
GIVETH A `May apply`
DECIDE `Can I apply now` IS
    `the s 17 answer` `another application for my injury is undecided` `I am an interim participant` `an earlier application was refused or my interim participation ended` `I give new or deterioration medical information` `I received a s 44(3)(a) payment` `the day I received the payment` `the years the regulation sets after a payment` `the regulation's circumstances apply to me` `the day I apply`

@export Can this person or insurer apply to the national injury insurance scheme for me?
GIVEN `who wants to apply` IS A `Who applies` @desc Who wants to apply: you yourself; an insurer against whom a CTP claim for your injury has been made; your parent or guardian; or another person
      `the claim was settled or decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an insurer: whether the claim has been settled by agreement or decided by a final judgment
      `a sanction of it is needed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that settlement or judgment must be approved (sanctioned) by a court or the public trustee
      `the sanction was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that sanction has been given
      `I am a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 18
      `they act for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person acts for you (for example as your attorney, administrator or other representative)
GIVETH A `Who may apply answer`
DECIDE `Can this person apply for me` IS
    CONSIDER `may apply under ss 16 and 18` `who wants to apply` (`the claim is finalised (s 10)` `the claim was settled or decided` FALSE `a sanction of it is needed` `the sanction was given`) `I am a child` `they act for me`
    WHEN JUST `yes` THEN
        IF `yes`
        THEN IF `who wants to apply` EQUALS `an insurer against whom a claim for the injury has been made`
             THEN `yes, the insurer may apply for me, and must give me a copy of the application (s 18(2))`
             ELSE `yes, this person may apply for me`
        ELSE `no: an insurer may apply only while its claim for my injury is not finalised (s 18(1)(a))`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the Act does not settle whether this person may apply for me`

@export Must the National Injury Insurance Agency accept me into the scheme, and for how long?
GIVEN `I am eligible under s 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are eligible to participate in the scheme for this injury (the eligibility question)
      `the agency is satisfied my injury will keep meeting the criteria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency is satisfied that your injury is likely to continue to meet the eligibility criteria after the interim participation period ends
      `I received a s 44(3)(a) payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or someone acting for you) have received a payment from the agency under s 44(3)(a) for this injury
      `the agency is satisfied I am in severe financial hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you received that payment: whether the agency is satisfied that you are suffering severe financial hardship
GIVETH AN `Application decision`
DECIDE `Must the agency accept me into the scheme` IS
    `the s 22 answer` `I am eligible under s 12` `the agency is satisfied my injury will keep meeting the criteria` `I received a s 44(3)(a) payment` `the agency is satisfied I am in severe financial hardship`

@export By when must the National Injury Insurance Agency decide my application, service request or payment request, and is it taken to be refused?
GIVEN `what I made` IS A `Request kind` @desc What you made: an application to participate in the scheme; a service request (asking the agency to fund treatment, care or support); or a payment request (asking it to pay an expense)
      `the day the agency received it` IS A DATE @desc The day the agency received it
      `the agency asked for more information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency sent an information request asking for further information
      `the day the agency asked` IS A DATE @desc The day of that information request (any date if none)
      `I gave the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the requested information has been given to the agency
      `the day I gave the information` IS A DATE @desc The day it was given (any date if not)
      `the days the agency extended the time` IS A NUMBER @desc For an application only: the number of days by which the agency, by notice, extended the time to decide (0 if none; the Act allows at most 28)
      `the agency has decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency has made its decision
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you want the answer for, usually today
GIVETH A `Decision status`
DECIDE `By when must the agency decide` IS
    `the decision status` `what I made` `the day the agency received it` `the agency asked for more information` `the day the agency asked` `I gave the information` `the day I gave the information` `the days the agency extended the time` `the agency has decided` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `Interim participation and becoming a lifetime participant (schedule 1, ss 45-48)`

@export When does my interim participation in the national injury insurance scheme end?
GIVEN `my day of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day I was accepted` IS A DATE @desc The day the agency accepted you as an interim participant
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When does my participation period end` IS
    `the last day of the participation period` `my day of birth` `the day I was accepted`

@export The agency plans to review my interim participation: by when must it give me notice of the review?
GIVEN `the day of the review` IS A DATE @desc The day the agency will carry out the review
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I be told of a review` IS
    `the last day for notice of a review (s 45(3))` `the day of the review`

@export The agency has decided the review of my interim participation: by when must it tell me?
GIVEN `the day of the review decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the agency made its decision after the review
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I be told the review decision` IS
    `the last day for notice of a review decision (s 47(1))` `the day of the review decision`

@export What happens at the end of my interim participation: do I become a lifetime participant, and if not, when does my participation end?
GIVEN `my day of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day I was accepted` IS A DATE @desc The day the agency accepted you as an interim participant
      `the agency decided the review before the period ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency made a decision after reviewing your participation before your participation period ended
      `the agency decided I am still eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it decided you are still eligible
      `the agency is satisfied my injury will continue to meet the criteria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is satisfied your injury is likely to keep meeting the eligibility criteria after the participation period
      `the notice states an earlier end day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice of the decision states an earlier day on which your participation ends
      `the earlier end day` IS A DATE @desc That earlier day (any date if none)
GIVETH AN `End of interim participation`
DECIDE `What happens at the end of my interim participation` IS
    `the s 46 answer` (`the last day of the participation period` `my day of birth` `the day I was accepted`) `the agency decided the review before the period ended` `the agency decided I am still eligible` `the agency is satisfied my injury will continue to meet the criteria` `the notice states an earlier end day` `the earlier end day`

§§ `Payment for treatment, care and support (ss 9, 35-37)`

@export Is this treatment, care or support "excluded" under the national injury insurance scheme, so that the agency ordinarily will not fund it?
GIVEN `it is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is provided without charge
      `I am a child and it is an ordinary cost of raising a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a child: whether it is something that ordinarily falls within the ordinary costs of raising a child
      `it is personal assistance or community participation care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is attendant care and support services that are personal assistance, or help to take part in the community
      `the regulation requires a registered provider for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulation requires this kind of care to be provided by a registered provider
      `it is provided by a hospital as part of its services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is provided to you at a hospital (as inpatient or outpatient) as part of the hospital's services
      `the provider is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider is on the agency's register of providers for that service
      `it is a medical trial or experimental` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is provided as part of a medical trial or on another experimental basis
      `it is a public sector health service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is provided as part of a public sector health service (a public hospital and health service)
      `it is provided by State emergency services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is provided by State emergency services such as the Queensland Ambulance Service or Queensland Fire and Rescue
      `the regulation excludes it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulation prescribes it as excluded
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this care excluded` IS
    `is excluded treatment, care and support (s 9)` (`Service facts` WITH
        `provided without charge` IS `it is free`
        `for a child, within the ordinary costs of raising a child` IS `I am a child and it is an ordinary cost of raising a child`
        `personal assistance or community participation attendant care` IS `it is personal assistance or community participation care`
        `prescribed by regulation as needing a registered provider` IS `the regulation requires a registered provider for it`
        `provided at a hospital as part of its services` IS `it is provided by a hospital as part of its services`
        `the provider is a registered provider` IS `the provider is registered`
        `part of a medical trial or experimental` IS `it is a medical trial or experimental`
        `part of a public sector health service` IS `it is a public sector health service`
        `provided by State emergency services` IS `it is provided by State emergency services`
        `prescribed by regulation as excluded` IS `the regulation excludes it`)

@export By when must I ask the National Injury Insurance Agency to pay an expense for my treatment, care or support?
GIVEN `the day I incurred the expense` IS A DATE @desc The day you incurred the expense
      `my funding agreement covers it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a funding agreement with the agency for this treatment, care or support that covers the period in which you incurred the expense
      `the day I ask` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or will make) the payment request
GIVETH A `Payment request timing`
DECIDE `By when must I make a payment request` IS
    `the s 35 answer` `the day I incurred the expense` `my funding agreement covers it` `the day I ask`

@export Must the agency approve my payment request, and how much must it pay?
GIVEN `I was a participant when I incurred it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a participant in the scheme when you incurred the expense
      `my participation was suspended when I incurred it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your participation was suspended (for an absence from Australia) when you incurred the expense
      `it is in my support plan or a service request approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the treatment, care or support is approved for you in your support plan (or, if you have no plan yet, in a service request approval)
      `it is excluded care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is excluded treatment, care and support (see the excluded-care question)
      `my plan or approval specifically includes it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is excluded: whether your support plan or service request approval specifically states that the agency will fund it
      `the amount I ask for` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you ask the agency to pay, in Australian dollars
      `a limit applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a limit applies: within Australia, an amount the regulation prescribes for this care; outside Australia, the average cost of the care in Queensland
      `the limit` IS A NUMBER @desc That limit, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Payment decision`
DECIDE `Must the agency approve my payment request` IS
    `the s 37 answer` `I was a participant when I incurred it` `my participation was suspended when I incurred it` `it is in my support plan or a service request approval` `it is excluded care` `my plan or approval specifically includes it` `the amount I ask for` `a limit applies` `the limit`

@export The agency approved my payment request: by when must it pay me?
GIVEN `the day of the approval` IS A DATE @desc The day the agency decided to approve the payment request
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the agency pay me` IS
    `the last day to pay (s 37(4))` `the day of the approval`

@export The agency asked me for information about my payment request: has the request lapsed?
GIVEN `the day the agency asked` IS A DATE @desc The day the agency gave you the information request
      `the due day in the request` IS A DATE @desc The due day the information request states
      `we agreed a later day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the agency agreed a later day
      `the later day agreed` IS A DATE @desc That later day (any date if none)
      `I gave the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the requested information has been given to the agency
      `the day I gave the information` IS A DATE @desc The day it was given (any date if not)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you want the answer for, usually today
GIVETH A `Lapse`
DECIDE `Has my payment request lapsed` IS
    `the s 36 answer` `the day the agency asked` `the due day in the request` `we agreed a later day` `the later day agreed` `I gave the information` `the day I gave the information` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `My damages claim against a CTP insurer (ss 40-44, 53)`

@export I have made a damages claim for my motor accident injury: must I tell the National Injury Insurance Agency, and by when?
GIVEN `I applied to the scheme or am a participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made the claim while your application to the scheme was undecided, or after you were accepted into the scheme
      `the day I made the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the claim
      `I told the agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the agency notice of the claim (that you made it, the day, and the insurer)
      `the day I told the agency` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave that notice (any date if not)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you want the answer for, usually today
GIVETH A `Claim notice`
DECIDE `Must I tell the agency about my claim` IS
    `the s 53 answer` `I applied to the scheme or am a participant` `the day I made the claim` `I told the agency` `the day I told the agency` `the day I am asking about`

@export As a lifetime participant with a CTP damages claim, by when must I tell the agency and the insurer whether I want to keep my right to treatment, care and support damages, and can I still do it?
GIVEN `I am a lifetime participant with a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a lifetime participant (not a buy-in participant) and a claim has been made against an insurer for your injury
      `a court made a s 43 order against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has ordered, on the agency's application under s 43, that you may not be awarded treatment, care and support damages
      `I made the claim after becoming a lifetime participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim was made after you were accepted as a lifetime participant
      `the day of the insurer's s 39 notice` IS A DATE @desc If the claim came after: the day you were given (or were entitled to be given) the insurer's notice under the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 s 39(1) or (2)
      `the day I was told I am a lifetime participant` IS A DATE @desc If the claim came before: the day you were given notice that you were accepted as a lifetime participant
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you want the answer for, usually today
      `a judgment or settlement has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a final judgment has been given, or a settlement made, on the claim
      `the insurer and the agency agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer and the agency agree to a late notice
      `my claim is in court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is the subject of a court proceeding
      `the court has allowed a late notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has ordered that the late notice may be given
GIVETH A `Preservation notice`
DECIDE `By when must I give my preservation notice` IS
    `the s 41 answer` `I am a lifetime participant with a claim` `a court made a s 43 order against me` `I made the claim after becoming a lifetime participant` `the day of the insurer's s 39 notice` `the day I was told I am a lifetime participant` `the day I am asking about` `a judgment or settlement has happened` `the insurer and the agency agree` `my claim is in court` `the court has allowed a late notice`

@export Is the National Injury Insurance Agency liable to contribute to the CTP insurer's liability for my treatment, care and support damages?
GIVEN `I gave a preservation notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the agency and the insurer a notice that you want to keep your right to treatment, care and support damages
      `contributory negligence was decided or agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court decided, or the parties agreed in a settlement, that you were contributorily negligent
      `the reduction for my contributory negligence, percent` IS A NUMBER @desc By what percentage your damages are reduced for that contributory negligence (for example 50; 0 if none)
      `a court refused to sanction my notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court decided under s 41(7) not to sanction (approve) your preservation notice
      `a court made a s 43 order against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has ordered under s 43 that you may not be awarded treatment, care and support damages
      `a court sanctioned my notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court sanctioned (approved) your preservation notice
      `I withdrew my notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you withdrew the preservation notice by notice to the agency and the insurer
GIVETH A `Contribution`
DECIDE `Is the agency liable to contribute to my damages` IS
    `the s 42 answer` `I gave a preservation notice` `contributory negligence was decided or agreed` `the reduction for my contributory negligence, percent` `a court refused to sanction my notice` `a court made a s 43 order against me` `a court sanctioned my notice` `I withdrew my notice`

@export I have been awarded treatment, care and support damages: by when must I tell the agency and the insurer whether I accept them?
GIVEN `how the damages were awarded` IS A `How damages were awarded` @desc How they were awarded: under a settlement or judgment that a court or the public trustee must sanction; under a binding settlement needing no sanction; or under a final court judgment needing no sanction
      `the day it starts from` IS A DATE @desc The day the sanction was given; or the day the settlement was made; or, for a judgment, the last day for lodging an appeal
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I say whether I accept my damages` IS
    `the last day of the acceptance period (s 44(8))` `how the damages were awarded` `the day it starts from`

@export What happens to my awarded treatment, care and support damages if I accept them, do not accept them, or have not yet said?
GIVEN `the agency must contribute to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were awarded treatment, care and support damages under a final judgment or binding settlement and the agency is liable to contribute towards them (see the contribution question)
      `my choice` IS AN `Acceptance choice` @desc What you told the agency and the insurer: that you accept the awarded damages; that you do not; or that you have not yet given notice
      `the damages awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The treatment, care and support damages awarded, in Australian dollars
      `the part for my time in the scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of them that relates to the period you have been a participant in the scheme, in Australian dollars
      `how the damages were awarded` IS A `How damages were awarded` @desc How they were awarded (see the acceptance-period question)
      `the day it starts from` IS A DATE @desc The day the sanction was given, the settlement made, or the appeal period ended
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you want the answer for, usually today
GIVETH AN `Awarded damages`
DECIDE `What happens to my awarded damages` IS
    `the s 44 answer` `the agency must contribute to them` `my choice` `the damages awarded` `the part for my time in the scheme` (`the last day of the acceptance period (s 44(8))` `how the damages were awarded` `the day it starts from`) `the day I am asking about`

§§ `Leaving Australia (ss 49-52) -- only if you are travelling overseas`

@export I am a participant and am going overseas: must I tell the National Injury Insurance Agency, and by when?
GIVEN `I will need care paid for while overseas that the agency did not plan for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while you are away, expenses are or are likely to be incurred for your treatment, care or support, and the agency did not consider care outside Australia when it decided your approved services
      `a service request or funding agreement covers my care abroad` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before you leave, a service request has been made, or a funding agreement entered into, for your care outside Australia
      `the day I leave` IS A DATE @desc The day you leave (or intend to leave) Australia
      `I told the agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the agency notice of the absence
      `the day I told the agency` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave that notice (any date if not)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you want the answer for, usually today
GIVETH AN `Absence notice`
DECIDE `Must I tell the agency before leaving Australia` IS
    `the s 50 answer` `I will need care paid for while overseas that the agency did not plan for` `a service request or funding agreement covers my care abroad` `the day I leave` `I told the agency` `the day I told the agency` `the day I am asking about`

@export Can the National Injury Insurance Agency suspend my participation in the scheme while I am overseas?
GIVEN `I am a buy-in participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a buy-in participant (accepted under s 13)
      `the day I leave` IS A DATE @desc The day you left Australia
      `the last day of my absence so far` IS A DATE @desc The day you came back, or today if you are still away
      `my claim` IS A `Claim position` @desc Your claim against a CTP insurer: none made; made, but the insurer denied liability or a court held it not liable; or made and liability not denied
      `the agency considers my absence will harm my condition or recovery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency considers your absence will, or is likely to, harm your condition or your prospects of improvement or rehabilitation
GIVETH A `Suspension`
DECIDE `Can the agency suspend my participation` IS
    `the s 52 answer` `I am a buy-in participant` `the day I leave` `the last day of my absence so far` `my claim` `the agency considers my absence will harm my condition or recovery`

§§ `Getting a decision reviewed (ss 105-129)`

@export By when must I apply to the National Injury Insurance Agency for internal review of its decision?
GIVEN `I was given the information notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given an information notice for the decision (a notice with the decision, reasons and review rights)
      `the day I was given it` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given it (any date if not)
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or will make) the internal review application
GIVETH AN `Internal review timing`
DECIDE `By when must I apply for internal review` IS
    `the s 107 answer` `I was given the information notice` `the day I was given it` `the day I apply`

@export By when must the agency decide my internal review, and is it taken to confirm the original decision?
GIVEN `the day the agency received my application` IS A DATE @desc The day the agency received your internal review application
      `the agency asked for more information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency sent an information request asking for further information
      `the day the agency asked` IS A DATE @desc The day of that information request (any date if none)
      `I gave the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the requested information has been given to the agency
      `the day I gave the information` IS A DATE @desc The day it was given (any date if not)
      `the agency has decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency has made its internal review decision
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you want the answer for, usually today
GIVETH AN `Internal review status`
DECIDE `By when must the agency decide my internal review` IS
    `the s 109 answer` `the day the agency received my application` `the agency asked for more information` `the day the agency asked` `I gave the information` `the day I gave the information` `the agency has decided` `the day I am asking about`

@export Can I have a medical question in my internal review decision referred to a medical tribunal, and by when must I ask?
GIVEN `the question decided` IS A `Medical matter` @desc What the internal review decision decided: whether the accident is the medical cause of the injury; whether the injury meets the eligibility criteria, on medical matters; whether an interim participant's injury will likely keep meeting them, on medical matters; another medical matter prescribed by regulation; or a matter that is not medical
      `the day the decision notice was given or due` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the decision notice for the internal review decision, or the day it was required to be given
      `the day I ask` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or will make) the referral request
GIVETH A `Medical tribunal referral`
DECIDE `Can I go to the medical tribunal` IS
    `the s 112 answer` `the question decided` `the day the decision notice was given or due` `the day I ask`

@export I am to attend before a medical tribunal: by when must I give it and the agency the documents I want considered?
GIVEN `the day I attend` IS A DATE @desc The day you are scheduled to attend before the medical tribunal
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc The public holidays (Queensland) between about three weeks before that day and that day, as dates; they are not business days
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I give my documents to the medical tribunal` IS
    `the last day to give documents to the medical tribunal (s 118(3))` `the day I attend` `the public holidays`

@export Can I apply to QCAT for review of the agency's internal review decision, and by when?
GIVEN `I applied for internal review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied to the agency for internal review of the decision
      `a medical question was referred to a medical tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a medical matter in the decision was referred to a medical tribunal
      `the day of the tribunal's notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the medical tribunal gave notice of its decision (any date if none)
GIVETH A `QCAT timing`
DECIDE `Can I apply to QCAT` IS
    `the s 127 answer` `I applied for internal review` `a medical question was referred to a medical tribunal` `the day of the tribunal's notice`

§§ `Offences (ss 50, 53, 132-134) -- only if you have been accused of one`

@export What is the most I can be penalised for an offence under the National Injury Insurance Scheme (Queensland) Act 2016?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence: not notifying the agency before leaving Australia (s 50); not telling the agency about a claim within 14 days (s 53); defrauding or deliberately misleading the agency (s 132); or giving information you know is false or misleading (s 133)
GIVETH A `Maximum penalty`
DECIDE `What is the most I can be penalised` IS
    `the maximum penalty` `the offence`

@export I gave the agency a document that was false or misleading: does the false-information offence not apply because I told the agency what was wrong and gave the correct information?
GIVEN `it was in a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information was given in a document
      `I told the agency how it is false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when giving it, you told the agency, as best you could, how the document is false or misleading
      `I have or can get the correct information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have, or can reasonably get, the correct information
      `I gave the correct information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the agency the correct information
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the false-information offence not apply to me` IS
    `s 133(1) does not apply (s 133(2))` `it was in a document` `I told the agency how it is false or misleading` `I have or can get the correct information` `I gave the correct information`

@export By when must a prosecution for an offence under the Act be started?
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence is said to have been committed
      `the day the complainant learned of it` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence came to the complainant's knowledge
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when can I be prosecuted` IS
    `the last day to start a prosecution (s 134(2))` `the day of the offence` `the day the complainant learned of it`
